{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn `origin/main` at `c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776`, `infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh` claims to prove the current review pipeline but checks only `LLM-Review` before submit. `infra/gerrit/project.config` also requires `Verified`. The script's test commit lacks the required `rebar-ticket:` trailer, so it no longer models an admissible production change.\n\n## Approach\nUpdate the live/manual E2E flow to create a valid ticket-linked commit and wait for both active gate votes before testing submit and replication. Keep credentials secret and cleanup bounded.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The test commit carries a resolvable full-canonical `rebar-ticket:` trailer and DCO sign-off.\n- [ ] The E2E fails unless both `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` are present on the tested patchset.\n- [ ] Submit and GitHub-replication assertions run only after both votes pass.\n- [ ] Existing credential-redaction, exit-code, and cleanup contracts remain intact.\n- [ ] Focused tests, shell checks, lint, and typecheck pass.\n\n## Plan-review remediation 2026-09-06\n\nThe CI trigger prerequisite for `Verified +1` is verified in-session with observable proxies, not by relying on a live Gerrit run in unit tests:\n\n- The script's Gerrit polling logic will parse the current patchset's labels and require `Verified.recommended` (or equivalent `+1`) in addition to `LLM-Review +1` before leaving the wait loop.\n- A focused script test will feed stubbed Gerrit change JSON where `LLM-Review` is +1 but `Verified` is absent/0 and assert the E2E does **not** proceed to submit. A second fixture with both labels +1 asserts submit is attempted.\n- A focused static/parser test will assert the generated test commit body contains a resolvable full canonical `rebar-ticket:` trailer plus `Signed-off-by`, using an isolated disposable ticket fixture unless the script is running in the external live integration mode.\n- The live script remains the external integration test: it may create/use a live disposable ticket because the operator ruling allows live-store access only for external integration tests. Non-external tests use stubs/fixtures and must not mutate the live store.\n\nUpdated verification commands:\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" bash -n infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_reviewbot_e2e.py` (or the existing focused test file that owns this script)\n- Safety grep proving the old single-vote wait did not survive: search the script/tests for the submit path and assert both `LLM-Review` and `Verified` gates are present before submit.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788764832936456001,"uuid":"68439ae2-9570-48de-a54e-3481a86ad87e"}